      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2011 American Society of Law, Medicine & Ethics, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "In early 2010, the Nebraska state legislature passed a new abortion restricting law asserting a new, compelling state interest in preventing fetal pain. In this article, we review existing constitutional abortion doctrine and note difficulties presented by persistent legal attention to a socially derived viability construct. We then offer a substantive biological, ethical, and legal critique of the new fetal pain rationale."
      },
